  "title": "Duplicate search results for AN4899 on st.com",
  "content": "<figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/6b205181-0c83-49cf-8e17-39decf45ae4c.png\" /></figure><p><a href=\"https://search.st.com/?activeSource=%22Search%22&amp;queryText=%22STM32%20microcontroller%20GPIO%20hardware%20settings%20and%20low-power%20consumption%22&amp;language=%22en%22&amp;pageSearch=1&amp;pageXRef=1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://search.st.com/?activeSource=%22Search%22&amp;queryText=%22STM32%20microcontroller%20GPIO%20hardware%20settings%20and%20low-power%20consumption%22&amp;language=%22en%22&amp;pageSearch=1&amp;pageXRef=1</a></p><p> </p><p>Although those two hits give slightly different titles, different URLs, and show different versions, they are, in fact, both AN4899 Rev 4:</p><p> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/853dec29-e913-4882-9b49-b415c67ac140.png\" /></figure><p><a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an4899-stm32-microcontroller-gpio-hardware-settings-and-lowpower-consumption-stmicroelectronics.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an4899-stm32-microcontroller-gpio-hardware-settings-and-lowpower-consumption-stmicroelectronics.pdf</a></p><p> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/1b2c40d5-2567-48b0-a76d-f0038e65e1e2.png\" /></figure><p><a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an4899-guidelines-for-gpio-hardware-settings-and-lowpower-consumption-on-stm32-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/an4899-guidelines-for-gpio-hardware-settings-and-lowpower-consumption-on-stm32-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf</a></p><p> </p><p> </p><p>And why does neither of the hits give the AN4899 reference?</p>",
